' ClassicDesktop — REALbasic / legacy API 1 desktop window, container, push-button,
' text-selection and drag-and-drop adapters over Buoy's UI runtime and the
' bundled legacy shim.
'
' Source rewrite for converted projects: Buoy's own `Window` is a different class
' from API 1's, so API 1 window classes inherit `ClassicWindow`, container
' controls inherit `ClassicContainerControl`, and push buttons that use
' `Default`/`Cancel` become `ClassicPushButton`. The members and event handlers
' inside keep their API 1 names (`Open`, `CancelClose(appQuitting)`, `Minimize`,
' `SelStart`, `AcceptTextDrop`, `DropObject`, …).
'
' Also: API 1 Edit-command routing and contextual Edit items over the native
' selection, ClassicQuit(exitCode)/ClassicExitCode, launch-document routing,
' and an error handler for exceptions raised from native callbacks.
'
' Native behavior is real where it is implemented and raises
' UnsupportedOperationException where it is not; see notes/desktop.md for the
' per-platform matrix and the gaps that need core runtime hooks.

Import RBFoundation
' One-way: ClassicListNative imports only legacy. A focused native list gets
' Return/Escape before the Default/Cancel buttons (API 1 KeyDown order).
Import ClassicListNative
Import ClassicListNative.{ ClassicListNativeSetDeclinedKeyHandler, ClassicListNativeOwnsKeys }

' ── Native bindings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

#If TargetLinux Then
    ' GtkTextIter is an opaque 80-byte stack struct on 64-bit GTK 4; reserve more.
    Sequential Structure ClassicTextIter
        A0 As Int64
        A1 As Int64
        A2 As Int64
        A3 As Int64
        A4 As Int64
        A5 As Int64
        A6 As Int64
        A7 As Int64
        A8 As Int64
        A9 As Int64
        A10 As Int64
        A11 As Int64
    End Structure

